endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (The design implements a 3-to-8 decoder hierarchically using two 2-to-4 decoder modules. The most significant select bit \(sel[2]\) determines which 2-to-4 decoder is enabled. When sel[2] = 0, the lower decoder is enabled, and when sel[2] = 1, the upper decoder is enabled. Both decoders receive the lower two select bits \(sel[1:0]\) as inputs. Since only one decoder is enabled at a time, only one output bit is asserted, producing a one-hot 8-bit output. The outputs of the two decoders are concatenated to form the final output vector y[7:0].)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (The testbench exhaustively tests all eight possible select values with the decoder enabled and verifies that the correct one-hot output is generated. It also checks that when the enable signal is deasserted, all outputs remain 0. PASS/FAIL messages are displayed for every test case, and a waveform is generated for visual verification.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (The waveform confirms the correct operation of the decoder. During the first half of the simulation, en is held low while sel cycles through all eight input combinations. As expected, the output y remains 00000000 for every select value, showing that the decoder is properly disabled.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (In the second half of the simulation, en is asserted high. As sel changes from 000 to 111, the output changes sequentially from 00000001 to 10000000. At every instant, exactly one output bit is high, demonstrating the expected one-hot decoding behavior)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (The terminal output displays a PASS message for every test case. When the decoder is disabled \(en = 0\), every output is correctly reported as 00000000. When the decoder is enabled \(en = 1\), the output matches the expected one-hot value for each select input. Since all test cases pass, the implementation correctly satisfies he functional requirements of a 3-to-8 decoder.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
